# AGENTS.md, Enforcement & Tooling → Process:
#
#   "Protected `main`. Merges only via PR with at least one approval;
#    `Modules/Billing` and `Modules/Dispatch` require a CODEOWNERS-designated
#    reviewer."
#
# This file is only half of that rule. GitHub will *request* a review from
# the owners below automatically, but it will not *require* one until
# "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in the branch protection rule
# for `main`. Without that setting this file is advisory, which is how
# thirteen commits reached `main` unreviewed on 1 Aug 2026.
#
# Setting it: Settings → Branches → Branch protection rules → main →
#   [x] Require a pull request before merging
#   [x] Require approvals (1)
#   [x] Require review from Code Owners
#   [x] Do not allow bypassing the above settings
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the two money modules are listed last.

